<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince-elector</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as electors</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A prince-elector was one of the princes entitled to elect the King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> fixed their number at seven: the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margrave-of-brandenburg">Margrave of Brandenburg</a>. The electoral system institutionalised the elective character of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-elector.jpg" alt="Prince-elector" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balduineum_Wahl_Heinrich_VII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
